# Round XXII Track δ regression: `take_int(None())` — the CALL form of the
# NoneLiteral at a function-argument position — must REJECT at check time.
# Same class as `int a = None()`, different position on the class-fix's axis.
# Runtime observed at HEAD 0aa3f5a6 pre-fix: `take_int` prints `got 0`, both
# backends agreeing on wrong output (Core #8 both-wrong).
#
# POSITION AXIS: fn-arg. Sibling `sound_bare_none_call_in_vardecl_rejected.gg`
# covers the var-decl position.

void take_int(int x): print(f"got {x}")

void main():
    take_int(None())
